## AppShell.Header (Recommended)
The most common approach is using `AppShell.Header` as part of Mantine's AppShell system:

```jsx
import { AppShell, Burger, Group, Text } from '@mantine/core';

function App() {
  return (
    <AppShell
      header={{ height: 60 }}
      padding="md"
    >
      <AppShell.Header>
        <Group h="100%" px="md">
          <Burger opened={opened} onClick={toggle} size="sm" />
          <Text size="lg" fw={500}>Your App</Text>
        </Group>
      </AppShell.Header>

      <AppShell.Main>
        {/* Your content */}
      </AppShell.Main>
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

## Custom Header Component
You can also create a standalone header component:

```jsx
import { Header, Group, Text, Box } from '@mantine/core';

function CustomHeader() {
  return (
    <Box
      style={{
        position: 'sticky',
        top: 0,
        zIndex: 100,
        backgroundColor: 'var(--mantine-color-body)',
        borderBottom: '1px solid var(--mantine-color-gray-3)'
      }}
      p="md"
    >
      <Group justify="space-between">
        <Text size="lg" fw={500}>Your App</Text>
        {/* Navigation items */}
      </Group>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

## Benefits of Using Components:
- **Consistency**: Maintains design system standards
- **Responsive**: Automatic responsive behavior
- **Theme integration**: Works seamlessly with Mantine's theming
- **Accessibility**: Built-in ARIA attributes and keyboard navigation
- **Layout management**: Proper spacing and positioning

The `AppShell.Header` is generally recommended as it provides the best integration with Mantine's layout system and handles responsive behavior automatically.

