 The issue is that you're using Mantine 8.0.1, but you haven't imported and configured the required CSS and theme provider that Mantine 8.0 needs. In Mantine 8.0, you need to set up the MantineProvider and import the core styles.

## Solution: Set up Mantine properly

### 1. Import Mantine CSS in your root layout or _app.js

If you're using Next.js 13+ with app directory, add this to your `app/layout.tsx`:

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import '@mantine/core/styles.css';
import { ColorSchemeScript, MantineProvider } from '@mantine/core';

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" suppressHydrationWarning>
      <head>
        <ColorSchemeScript />
      </head>
      <body>
        <MantineProvider>{children}</MantineProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

### 2. Or if you're using pages directory, add to `_app.tsx`:

```tsx
// pages/_app.tsx
import '@mantine/core/styles.css';
import type { AppProps } from 'next/app';
import { MantineProvider } from '@mantine/core';

export default function App({ Component, pageProps }: AppProps) {
  return (
    <MantineProvider>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </MantineProvider>
  );
}
```

### 3. Your component should work after this setup:

```tsx
// Your Demo.tsx file (this should work once MantineProvider is set up)
import { Group, Button, AppShell } from '@mantine/core';

export function Demo() {
  return (
    <Group>
      <Button color="sugar-milk" variant="filled">
        Sugar Milk button
      </Button>
      <Button>Default button</Button>
    </Group>
  );
}

export function Demo2() {
  return (
    <AppShell header={{ height: 48 }}>
      <AppShell.Header>Header</AppShell.Header>
      <AppShell.Main>Main content</AppShell.Main>
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

## Alternative: Check if you need to add PostCSS config

If you're still having issues, you might need PostCSS configuration. Create `postcss.config.js`:

```js
// postcss.config.js
module.exports = {
  plugins: {
    'postcss-preset-mantine': {},
    'postcss-simple-vars': {
      variables: {
        'mantine-breakpoint-xs': '36em',
        'mantine-breakpoint-sm': '48em',
        'mantine-breakpoint-md': '62em',
        'mantine-breakpoint-lg': '75em',
        'mantine-breakpoint-xl': '88em',
      },
    },
  },
};
```

And install the required packages:

```bash
npm install --save-dev postcss postcss-preset-mantine postcss-simple-vars
```

The key issue is that Mantine 8.0 requires the `MantineProvider` wrapper and CSS imports to function properly. Once you add those, `AppShell.Header` should work correctly!

