chat_messages.text:
 Ah, that makes perfect sense! You discovered the issue - **AppShell requires client-side rendering** in Next.js 13+ with the app router.

## Why This Happens

In Next.js 13+ with the app router, components are server-rendered by default. AppShell has interactive features and uses hooks internally, so it needs to run on the client side.

## Best Practices for Mantine + Next.js App Router

### 1. Add 'use client' to pages that use interactive Mantine components:

```tsx
'use client';

import { Group, Button, AppShell } from '@mantine/core';

export function Demo() {
  return (
    <Group>
      <Button color="sugar-milk" variant="filled">
        Sugar Milk button
      </Button>
      <Button>Default button</Button>
    </Group>
  );
}

export function Demo2() {
  return (
    <AppShell header={{ height: 48 }}>
      <AppShell.Header>Header</AppShell.Header>
      <AppShell.Main>Main content</AppShell.Main>
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

### 2. Or create separate client components:

```tsx
// components/ClientAppShell.tsx
'use client';

import { AppShell } from '@mantine/core';

interface Props {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

export function ClientAppShell({ children }: Props) {
  return (
    <AppShell header={{ height: 48 }}>
      <AppShell.Header>Header</AppShell.Header>
      <AppShell.Main>{children}</AppShell.Main>
    </AppShell>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// app/sample/page.tsx (can remain server component)
import { ClientAppShell } from '@/components/ClientAppShell';

export default function SamplePage() {
  return (
    <ClientAppShell>
      <div>Server-rendered content can go here</div>
    </ClientAppShell>
  );
}
```

### 3. Components that typically need 'use client':
- `AppShell` (uses layout state)
- `Drawer`, `Modal` (use portals)
- `Menu`, `Popover` (use floating UI)
- Form components with validation
- Components using hooks like `useDisclosure`, `useForm`

### 4. Components that work in server components:
- `Button`, `Text`, `Title`
- `Container`, `Group`, `Stack`
- `Card`, `Paper`
- Most layout and display components

Great catch! This is a common gotcha when migrating to the Next.js app router with Mantine.

