chat_messages.text:
 To set the default font for Mantine, you need to configure it in your theme. Here are the different ways to do it:

## Option 1: Set Global Font in Your Theme (Recommended)

Update your `theme.ts` file:

```ts
// theme.ts
import { createTheme } from '@mantine/core';

export const theme = createTheme({
  fontFamily: 'Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif',
  // You can also set specific font families for different text types
  fontFamilyMonospace: 'Monaco, Courier, monospace',
  headings: {
    fontFamily: 'Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif',
  },
});
```

## Option 2: Using Google Fonts

First, add the font to your layout:

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import '@mantine/core/styles.css';
import { ColorSchemeScript, MantineProvider } from '@mantine/core';
import { theme } from '../theme';

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <head>
        <ColorSchemeScript />
        {/* Add Google Font */}
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossOrigin="anonymous" />
        <link 
          href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" 
          rel="stylesheet" 
        />
      </head>
      <body>
        <MantineProvider theme={theme}>{children}</MantineProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

Then update your theme:

```ts
// theme.ts
import { createTheme } from '@mantine/core';

export const theme = createTheme({
  fontFamily: 'Inter, sans-serif',
  headings: {
    fontFamily: 'Inter, sans-serif',
  },
});
```

## Option 3: Using Next.js Font Optimization

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import '@mantine/core/styles.css';
import { ColorSchemeScript, MantineProvider } from '@mantine/core';
import { Inter } from 'next/font/google';
import { theme } from '../theme';

const inter = Inter({ 
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
});

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={inter.className}>
      <head>
        <ColorSchemeScript />
      </head>
      <body>
        <MantineProvider theme={theme}>{children}</MantineProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

```ts
// theme.ts
import { createTheme } from '@mantine/core';

export const theme = createTheme({
  fontFamily: 'var(--font-inter), sans-serif',
  headings: {
    fontFamily: 'var(--font-inter), sans-serif',
  },
});
```

## Option 4: Different Fonts for Different Elements

```ts
// theme.ts
import { createTheme } from '@mantine/core';

export const theme = createTheme({
  // Default font for body text
  fontFamily: 'Inter, sans-serif',

  // Font for headings
  headings: {
    fontFamily: 'Roboto, sans-serif',
  },

  // Font for monospace elements (code, etc.)
  fontFamilyMonospace: 'Fira Code, Monaco, Courier, monospace',

  // You can also override font families for specific components
  components: {
    Button: {
      defaultProps: {
        styles: {
          root: {
            fontFamily: 'Inter, sans-serif',
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

## Option 5: Using CSS Variables

You can also set fonts using CSS variables in your global CSS:

```css
/* globals.css */
:root {
  --mantine-font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
  --mantine-font-family-monospace: 'Monaco', 'Courier New', monospace;
  --mantine-font-family-headings: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
}
```

## Popular Font Combinations

Here are some popular font choices:

```ts
// Modern/Clean
fontFamily: 'Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif',

// Professional
fontFamily: 'Roboto, Arial, sans-serif',

// Elegant
fontFamily: 'Source Sans Pro, Arial, sans-serif',

// Tech/Startup
fontFamily: 'Nunito Sans, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif',

// Classic
fontFamily: 'Open Sans, Arial, sans-serif',
```

**I recommend Option 1 or Option 3** as they provide the best integration with Mantine's theme system and Next.js optimization!

