# Base Theme Configuration Setup for Chakra UI 3.17

This guide provides a comprehensive, step-by-step approach to setting up a base theme configuration using Chakra UI 3.17 in a Next.js project with TypeScript.

## Table of Contents

1. [Introduction](#introduction)
2. [Project Structure](#project-structure)
3. [Base Setup](#base-setup)
4. [Theme Configuration](#theme-configuration)
5. [Recipes for Component Variants](#recipes-for-component-variants)
6. [Provider Setup](#provider-setup)
7. [Component Implementation](#component-implementation)
8. [Usage Examples](#usage-examples)
9. [Best Practices](#best-practices)

## Introduction

Chakra UI 3.17 introduces significant changes to the theming system, moving from the Theme Provider approach to a system-based architecture using `createSystem`. This guide demonstrates how to build a flexible theme system leveraging these new capabilities.

## Project Structure

Here's the recommended file structure for theme configuration:

```
/project-root
  /theme
    /recipes
      button.ts
      card.ts
      input.ts
      ... other component recipes
    colors.ts
    tokens.ts
    semantic-tokens.ts
    index.ts
  /components
    /ui
      button.tsx
      card.tsx
      provider.tsx
      ... other UI components
  /app
    layout.tsx
    page.tsx
```

## Base Setup

### 1. Install Dependencies

First, ensure you have the necessary dependencies installed:

```bash
npm install @chakra-ui/react
```

### 2. Create Base Theme Files

We'll start by creating the foundation files for our theme system.

#### `theme/tokens.ts`

This file defines our base design tokens:

