 Fair enough! Here's a simple but secure approach that actually works in Power Apps:

## Multi-Click Security (Click π exactly 5 times)

```
Set(AdminClicks, AdminClicks + 1);
Set(LastClickTime, Now());
If(
    AdminClicks = 5,
    Set(IsAdminMode, !IsAdminMode);
    Set(AdminClicks, 0);
    Notify("Admin mode " & If(IsAdminMode, "activated", "deactivated"), NotificationType.Success),
    Notify("Click " & (5 - AdminClicks) & " more times", NotificationType.Information)
);
```

**App OnStart:**
```
Set(IsAdminMode, false);
Set(AdminClicks, 0)
```

## How It Works:
- Click π **exactly 5 times** = Admin mode toggles
- **Less than 5 clicks** = Shows "Click X more times"
- **More than 5 clicks** = Resets counter
- **Security through obscurity** - users won't know to click 5 times

## Alternative: Specific Click Pattern
**Click π 3 times, pause, then click 2 more times:**
```
Set(AdminClicks, AdminClicks + 1);
Set(LastClickTime, Now());
If(AdminClicks = 3, Set(PauseTimer, Now()));
If(
    AdminClicks = 5 && (Now() - PauseTimer) > TimeValue("00:00:01"),
    Set(IsAdminMode, !IsAdminMode);
    Set(AdminClicks, 0);
    Notify("Admin access granted", NotificationType.Success),
    If(AdminClicks > 5, Set(AdminClicks, 0))
)
```

**Which approach feels right to you?** The 5-click method is simple but reasonably secure for most use cases.

