 I found the problem! You have **two competing root layouts** that are both trying to render `<html>` and `<body>` tags:

1. `app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
2. `app/(admin)/admin/layout.tsx` (admin layout - **this is the problem**)

In Next.js, only the root `app/layout.tsx` should have `<html>` and `<body>` tags. All other layouts should just return the children with any wrapper components.

Your `app/(admin)/admin/layout.tsx` is trying to be a second root layout, which is breaking everything.

**Fix:** Update your `app/(admin)/admin/layout.tsx` to this:

```typescript
import { MantineProvider } from '@mantine/core';

export default function AdminLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <MantineProvider>
      {children}
    </MantineProvider>
  );
}
```

Remove the `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags from the admin layout - only keep the MantineProvider wrapper.

This should fix your layout issues! The dashboard layout will then work properly within this structure.

