chat_messages.text:
 Great question! Here's the key difference:

## **Default Export** (one per file)
```tsx
// In Footer.tsx
function Footer() {
  return <div>Footer content</div>;
}

export default Footer;
// OR
export default function Footer() {
  return <div>Footer content</div>;
}
```

**Import:**
```tsx
import Footer from './Footer';           // ✅ Works
import AnyName from './Footer';          // ✅ Also works - you can rename it
```

## **Named Export** (multiple per file)
```tsx
// In Footer.tsx
export function Footer() {
  return <div>Footer content</div>;
}

export function Header() {
  return <div>Header content</div>;
}
```

**Import:**
```tsx
import { Footer } from './Footer';       // ✅ Must use exact name
import { Footer, Header } from './Footer'; // ✅ Import multiple
import { Footer as MyFooter } from './Footer'; // ✅ Rename with 'as'
```

## **The Problem**
If your Footer component uses **named export** but you're importing it as **default export**, you get `undefined`:

```tsx
// If Footer.tsx has: export function Footer() {...}
import Footer from './Footer';  // ❌ Returns undefined!
```

**Check your Footer.tsx file** - does it have `export default Footer` or `export function Footer`? That will tell us which import style to use.

